WEBVTT

01:20.872 --> 01:21.706
I...

01:22.415 --> 01:23.583
got suspended.

01:24.542 --> 01:26.419
They're not going to
pay me during my suspension,

01:27.504 --> 01:29.380
and I'm probably going to get sued.

01:31.549 --> 01:33.343
Everything is so messed up.

01:35.595 --> 01:36.513
You said before

01:37.514 --> 01:38.890
you'll run away with me

01:39.933 --> 01:41.392
whenever I want.

01:45.313 --> 01:46.272
I want to

01:47.315 --> 01:48.441
go on a trip with you.

01:53.238 --> 01:54.072
Right now.

02:00.411 --> 02:01.246
Let's go.

02:26.020 --> 02:29.607
CHAPTER 9
KING DONKEY EARS

02:34.904 --> 02:35.947
Where should we go?

02:36.531 --> 02:38.449
Don't you think it'd be nice to go abroad?

02:38.533 --> 02:40.618
South America and Europe both sound nice.

02:42.036 --> 02:44.080
Let's go somewhere hotter than here.
How about Africa?

02:44.455 --> 02:46.833
Serengeti, the wildlife refuge.
What do you think?

02:53.172 --> 02:54.799
"What in the world have I done?"

02:59.345 --> 03:00.513
Is that...

03:01.639 --> 03:02.849
what you're thinking right now?

03:03.433 --> 03:06.102
No, not at all.

03:06.185 --> 03:07.937
You'd better not be thinking that.

03:08.521 --> 03:10.398
You impressed me by punching that guy

03:10.481 --> 03:12.025
and even asked me to take you on a trip.

03:12.317 --> 03:14.611
Don't tell me
you're starting to regret it.

03:15.278 --> 03:17.655
No, of course not.

03:18.406 --> 03:19.699
I'm not regretting it.

03:20.992 --> 03:22.035
Then let's go to Serengeti.

03:24.537 --> 03:25.914
I don't have a passport.

03:28.333 --> 03:29.792
Are you from outer space?

03:30.877 --> 03:33.296
- Who doesn't have a passport these days?
- Me. I don't.

03:35.715 --> 03:38.051
- We can go to Jeju Island.
- We won't be able to return today.

03:38.134 --> 03:39.636
"Return today"? Are you joking?

03:40.220 --> 03:42.680
Last time, you offered to take me
to a mountain or a field.

03:42.764 --> 03:44.015
That won't take more than a day.

03:44.807 --> 03:45.642
Okay, fine.

03:46.893 --> 03:47.727
Then for one night--

03:47.810 --> 03:49.687
If we're spending the night,
let's take Sang-tae.

03:55.693 --> 03:58.488
- What are you doing?
- Think carefully before you answer.

03:58.571 --> 03:59.656
Stop the car.

03:59.739 --> 04:02.617
Do you want to go for a day
or spend the night with me?

04:02.700 --> 04:03.576
Stop the car!

04:03.660 --> 04:05.161
Do you want to spend the night with me

04:06.329 --> 04:08.456
or die with me?

04:09.582 --> 04:10.959
Ko Mun-yeong!

04:22.387 --> 04:24.973
Are you nuts? Why would you risk your life
to joke around?

04:27.684 --> 04:28.768
Who says I'm joking around?

04:29.352 --> 04:33.022
Please. At least count to three
before you do anything impulsive.

04:35.066 --> 04:37.860
Did you count to three
before you punched that guy?

04:42.615 --> 04:43.616
Get out.

04:44.200 --> 04:45.785
If I stay with you,

04:45.868 --> 04:48.079
it'll make me
want to crash into something.

05:37.128 --> 05:39.964
Damn it! Gang-tae, that darn asshole!

05:40.256 --> 05:42.300
He wanted to go on a trip.
Is he teasing me or what?

05:45.636 --> 05:46.763
Is he really teasing me?

05:48.014 --> 05:50.099
What the heck? How dare he tease me?

05:51.017 --> 05:52.560
How am I going to get back at him?

06:02.445 --> 06:03.488
Hey, buddy.

06:04.322 --> 06:06.074
You're so strange these days.

06:07.325 --> 06:08.576
I didn't have lunch.

06:09.410 --> 06:10.787
You always skip meals,

06:10.870 --> 06:12.914
and you quit your job
like it's your hobby.

06:13.539 --> 06:16.626
But you punched someone today
and got suspended.

06:17.502 --> 06:19.545
I'm surprised you have an appetite.

06:25.134 --> 06:25.968
This is good.

06:27.678 --> 06:30.556
Buddy, you must be sick in the mind.

06:31.140 --> 06:32.767
Let's go get a checkup.

06:35.353 --> 06:38.272
- Do you also think I'm a little strange?
- Not just a little. Very.

06:41.859 --> 06:44.612
- What's the matter with me, Jae-su?
- It's the lunatic virus.

06:45.446 --> 06:46.906
- "A virus"?
- That day,

06:47.532 --> 06:51.285
when Ko Mun-yeong
hurt your hand with a knife,

06:51.494 --> 06:56.040
her lunatic virus must have
entered your blood vessels

06:56.124 --> 06:59.585
and totally messed up your brain.

07:06.008 --> 07:07.260
You almost convinced me.

07:07.343 --> 07:08.761
I almost thought of writing a novel.

07:10.847 --> 07:13.182
- Do you know the word for that in English?
- "In English"?

07:13.558 --> 07:15.309
Gosh, do you think I'm dumb?

07:16.477 --> 07:18.104
You want to know what it is in English?

07:18.187 --> 07:19.397
My gosh, come on.

07:19.480 --> 07:21.190
It's "Nobel" as in
Nobel Prize in Literature.

07:21.274 --> 07:23.192
My goodness, I guess you didn't know.

07:25.445 --> 07:28.990
Yes, novel. That's what I said.
Novel Prize in Literature.

07:29.073 --> 07:29.991
My gosh, seriously.

07:30.074 --> 07:32.452
Okay, fine. My pronunciation sucked.
I admit that, okay?

07:33.744 --> 07:35.246
- Jae-su.
- Yes, I know.

07:37.206 --> 07:38.332
Gosh, that's enough.

07:38.416 --> 07:39.876
End of conversation. Just drop it.

07:40.001 --> 07:40.835
I...

07:42.253 --> 07:43.296
want to have fun.

07:45.548 --> 07:47.091
Sure. Why not?

07:47.175 --> 07:50.136
It's been a while.
Let's go for a ride on Alberto.

07:50.219 --> 07:51.220
Where do you want to go?

07:54.765 --> 07:57.894
- Serengeti.
- Sereng... What?

07:58.895 --> 08:00.938
He's not that kind of person.

08:01.522 --> 08:03.983
He's a very patient guy.
I can't believe he punched someone.

08:04.066 --> 08:05.568
It's just like when you fart.

08:06.152 --> 08:07.945
If you hold it in 99 times

08:08.029 --> 08:10.781
and finally let it out,
it could kill people.

08:11.491 --> 08:13.534
You... You have no manners.

08:14.076 --> 08:15.745
Don't talk about farting
when we're eating.

08:16.329 --> 08:18.998
It's making me lose my appetite.

08:19.081 --> 08:20.958
I'm sorry. Sorry about that.

08:22.001 --> 08:25.213
Eat... Eat your own side dishes.

08:26.714 --> 08:29.967
But how did he end up punching someone?

08:30.051 --> 08:33.554
Back in the days,
I also beat up guys who used to bully you.

08:33.638 --> 08:35.723
He probably got angry for the same reason.

08:36.474 --> 08:39.143
Back when I was young,
I had a crush on Sun-deok.

08:39.393 --> 08:40.895
But I got rejected three times.

08:41.395 --> 08:43.397
That's... That's quite a surprise.

08:43.481 --> 08:45.983
But... But how did you reject him?

08:46.317 --> 08:48.110
"I don't like you!
I really don't like you!"

08:48.402 --> 08:49.612
That's how I rejected him.

08:49.904 --> 08:53.282
He was very unusual
ever since he was young.

08:53.491 --> 08:54.784
It was a 50-50 chance.

08:54.867 --> 08:57.620
He was either a genius or an idiot,
so I just rejected him.

08:58.788 --> 09:00.414
You regret it, don't you?

09:00.498 --> 09:02.625
My goodness, how did you know?

09:02.875 --> 09:05.169
I regret it very much.

09:06.337 --> 09:07.964
Don't leave any food on your plate.

09:09.507 --> 09:10.550
Did you see that?

09:10.633 --> 09:12.718
She still has feelings for me.

09:12.802 --> 09:14.845
Don't be delusional. Drink your soup.

09:18.307 --> 09:19.308
Director.

09:21.936 --> 09:23.854
I'm sorry for bothering you
during your meal.

09:24.355 --> 09:25.898
But can you come with me for a moment?

09:27.191 --> 09:28.484
What's going on?

09:29.151 --> 09:30.695
- You can keep eating.
- Okay.

09:33.614 --> 09:35.199
Why can't she get discharged?

09:35.283 --> 09:37.118
We're not saying she can't get discharged.

09:37.201 --> 09:38.995
- But there's a procedure--
- I don't care.

09:39.662 --> 09:41.956
- Let's go.
- Please calm down.

09:42.039 --> 09:44.792
- The director will be here--
- How do you expect us to calm down?

09:44.959 --> 09:46.002
Her ex-husband...

09:47.295 --> 09:49.964
We brought her to this hospital
so that jerk wouldn't find her.

09:50.047 --> 09:52.758
But that lunatic managed to find her here.

09:54.302 --> 09:56.971
You should just come with me
to the States.

09:57.054 --> 09:58.764
You can get treated there.

09:58.848 --> 10:00.850
No, I don't want to go.
Just go by yourself.

10:00.933 --> 10:02.476
Stop complaining! Let's go!

10:04.770 --> 10:06.355
If you must leave...

10:10.568 --> 10:12.320
What? What do you want?

10:13.904 --> 10:15.948
Our hospital administration
is handled over there.

10:16.032 --> 10:17.867
You need to pay before you go.

10:20.911 --> 10:23.414
- You need to pay.
- We'll pay, okay?

10:23.497 --> 10:25.082
- Let's go, Mom.
- My goodness.

10:26.083 --> 10:28.586
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

10:30.046 --> 10:31.631
Hurry up. Come on.

10:33.049 --> 10:36.552
Ms. Lee A-reum isn't ready
to get discharged.

10:37.720 --> 10:39.513
Are you really going to let her leave?

10:42.850 --> 10:45.311
What else can we do to stop her
from leaving?

10:46.479 --> 10:48.773
Her family won't let her stay.

10:54.320 --> 10:55.613
- Come here.
- What is it?

10:55.696 --> 10:56.781
Be quiet.

10:57.156 --> 10:59.825
Jeong-tae. Listen to me carefully.

11:00.076 --> 11:01.118
I'm listening.

11:02.536 --> 11:04.914
You see, A-reum...

11:04.997 --> 11:06.082
What about her?

11:06.332 --> 11:09.001
Well, the thing is, A-reum...

11:09.585 --> 11:11.504
No! A-reum...

11:18.803 --> 11:20.930
Hey, Jeong-tae.

11:21.597 --> 11:25.434
You shouldn't let people find out
that you and A-reum are a couple.

11:26.018 --> 11:27.895
So just try your best to hold it in.

11:28.521 --> 11:31.107
- I'll try to find a way.
- Damn it.

11:34.652 --> 11:35.736
Jeong-tae.

11:36.320 --> 11:40.574
Tomorrow, someone who can help you
will show up from the west.

11:41.158 --> 11:42.827
What? A ghost from the west?

11:42.910 --> 11:46.414
Someone who can help him
will show up from the west.

11:46.539 --> 11:48.624
A person. Not a ghost.

11:48.707 --> 11:51.335
He snores, grinds his teeth, and farts.

11:51.419 --> 11:53.712
He does it all simultaneously.
It's like a darn orchestra.

11:56.590 --> 12:00.261
I bet every single hole
in Lee Sang-in's body opens up

12:00.594 --> 12:03.514
when that guy goes to sleep.

12:05.015 --> 12:06.767
My gosh, it's hilarious.

12:07.810 --> 12:09.728
If you can't stand him,
you can sleep in our room.

12:09.812 --> 12:11.230
- It's empty.
- Can I really do that?

12:14.984 --> 12:17.486
- I also have a favor to ask you.
- "A favor"?

12:19.572 --> 12:21.615
It's regarding Sang-tae.
Tomorrow, can you--

12:21.699 --> 12:22.825
Sure.

12:23.826 --> 12:26.162
- But I'm not done talking.
- There's no need to explain.

12:26.745 --> 12:28.956
I'll help you out no matter what.

12:29.039 --> 12:30.791
That's what you call loyalty.

12:32.209 --> 12:33.043
Thanks.

12:34.628 --> 12:36.005
Then who do you like more? Me or Sang-tae?

12:37.298 --> 12:39.341
- Do I really need to answer that?
- What?

12:41.510 --> 12:42.470
I'll see you.

12:48.893 --> 12:50.144
I like you, too.

12:54.440 --> 12:57.485
- "Those two guys are
- Those two guys are

12:57.568 --> 13:00.029
- trying to take over our house.
- trying to take over our house.

13:00.112 --> 13:02.072
- They're a pair of rascals."
- They're a pair of rascals.

13:02.156 --> 13:03.115
I hate them.

13:05.326 --> 13:07.536
I really hate Dooly and his friends.

13:08.454 --> 13:11.123
It's not even their house,
but they do whatever they want.

13:12.500 --> 13:13.667
I like Ko Gil-dong.

13:15.628 --> 13:16.629
"Ko Gil-dong"?

13:17.296 --> 13:20.257
He let those guys into his territory.

13:21.383 --> 13:23.802
He's a nice guy.

13:25.429 --> 13:27.431
- What do you think?
- I like him.

13:28.641 --> 13:31.268
I... I also like Gil-dong.

13:31.352 --> 13:35.064
This... This guy's name is Teary.
His real name is Ko Gil-dong.

13:35.147 --> 13:37.775
His name is Teary. This right here
is actually a piece of thread,

13:37.858 --> 13:39.818
but it's also a teardrop.
His name is Ko Gil-dong.

13:40.653 --> 13:42.029
- Do you also like him?
- Yes.

13:42.112 --> 13:45.574
Ko Gil-dong is a caregiver
for Dooly, Douner, and Ddochi.

13:45.658 --> 13:48.827
I mean, he's their guardian,
and he gives them a place to sleep,

13:48.911 --> 13:51.330
gives them food, and protects them.

13:51.413 --> 13:53.999
Just for your information,
I'm Gang-tae's guardian.

13:54.083 --> 13:57.169
And a guardian should be
dependable and trustworthy.

13:57.253 --> 14:00.422
I'm an adult and his older brother.
That's who I am.

14:08.097 --> 14:09.265
We really click, Sang-tae.

14:09.974 --> 14:11.267
We're like best friends.

14:16.105 --> 14:17.231
"Best friends"?

14:20.359 --> 14:21.318
Best friends.

14:23.279 --> 14:24.363
My gosh, we're best friends.

14:24.446 --> 14:26.448
Yes, best friends.

14:27.157 --> 14:28.659
Best friends.

14:32.037 --> 14:33.497
Sang-tae, I'm home.

14:43.340 --> 14:44.300
Can we talk?

14:47.469 --> 14:49.305
Best friends.

14:58.564 --> 15:00.065
Are we not going anywhere tomorrow?

15:02.776 --> 15:06.196
Did you overreact like that earlier
to have fun for just one day?

15:08.032 --> 15:09.491
One day is more than enough for me.

15:10.951 --> 15:12.244
I dreamt of that day

15:14.496 --> 15:16.540
my entire life.

15:24.715 --> 15:25.716
You're so annoying.

15:28.761 --> 15:30.220
So are we going tomorrow?

15:31.680 --> 15:32.514
Sometimes,

15:33.849 --> 15:36.060
you're like a tamer, not a caregiver.

15:36.977 --> 15:37.811
"A tamer"?

15:37.895 --> 15:40.856
I feel like you're taming me.

15:48.280 --> 15:49.865
I think it's the opposite.

15:54.078 --> 15:55.704
I keep doing things I wouldn't normally do

15:57.915 --> 15:59.458
because of you.

16:02.378 --> 16:03.253
Earlier,

16:05.339 --> 16:06.340
I couldn't hear

16:08.801 --> 16:10.135
or see anything.

16:16.809 --> 16:18.060
I must have been out of my mind.

16:21.814 --> 16:23.273
I really couldn't hold my anger.

16:25.317 --> 16:27.277
No, you weren't out of your mind.

16:32.116 --> 16:33.283
You were stunning.

17:09.445 --> 17:12.656
Should we leave the house
tomorrow morning?

17:13.240 --> 17:14.950
Yes, sure.

17:16.201 --> 17:17.327
Good night.

17:25.502 --> 17:28.172
I want to twist that deer's neck.

17:29.465 --> 17:30.507
Shut up, you stupid deer!

18:02.790 --> 18:03.832
Ju-ri.

18:05.709 --> 18:06.794
Where are you going?

18:13.467 --> 18:14.885
Seung-jae.

18:16.220 --> 18:17.971
Have you ever been in a one-sided love?

18:19.139 --> 18:21.892
No, I would never do something so dumb.

18:21.975 --> 18:23.185
It's such a waste of time.

18:26.355 --> 18:27.397
I know, right?

18:29.358 --> 18:30.192
It's a waste of time.

18:31.068 --> 18:32.694
You deserve way better.

18:34.696 --> 18:37.032
- Do you know who I have a crush on?
- Mr. Moon Gang-tae.

18:38.450 --> 18:42.496
I'm very slow when it comes to work.

18:43.288 --> 18:46.333
But when it comes to love,
I'm very quick-witted.

18:49.628 --> 18:51.880
Let's be honest and realistic.

18:51.964 --> 18:53.966
You're a lot better than Mr. Moon.

18:54.174 --> 18:57.136
He may be good-looking,
but he has absolutely nothing...

19:01.849 --> 19:02.766
You're right.

19:05.435 --> 19:07.062
He doesn't have anything to offer.

19:10.232 --> 19:12.276
He really doesn't.

19:14.695 --> 19:16.113
I must've thought

19:19.908 --> 19:22.578
I could be the one to fill up

19:26.039 --> 19:27.416
his empty life.

19:30.794 --> 19:32.045
What's the matter with me?

19:39.553 --> 19:40.721
I must be drunk.

19:41.513 --> 19:43.056
Let's go inside after we finish this.

19:48.896 --> 19:50.939
I personally think
you should be with a guy

19:51.690 --> 19:55.402
who's older than you, and has a laid-back

19:56.195 --> 20:00.240
and broad-minded personality,
with the characteristics of a businessman.

20:01.366 --> 20:03.994
I'm sure you'll be able to find
a guy like that somewhere nearby.

20:23.972 --> 20:25.933
She's finally doing her money's worth.

20:33.065 --> 20:34.858
No, you weren't out of your mind.

20:35.943 --> 20:37.069
You were stunning.

20:38.737 --> 20:39.780
I must be out of my mind.

20:41.406 --> 20:42.574
What?

20:44.326 --> 20:46.036
No, it's nothing. Go back to bed.

20:47.412 --> 20:49.122
- Go back to sleep.
- Okay.

20:53.168 --> 20:55.545
If you're out of your mind,
you need to go to a hospital.

20:56.129 --> 20:57.714
It means you're sick.

21:25.242 --> 21:26.618
I must have been out of my mind.

21:27.661 --> 21:29.162
I really couldn't hold my anger.

21:30.539 --> 21:32.582
He shouldn't have held back
his desire either.

21:33.834 --> 21:34.793
My gosh.

21:51.977 --> 21:54.813
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

21:54.896 --> 21:55.731
DIRECTOR O'S MUSIC CLASS

21:55.814 --> 21:59.151
- It's okay to not be okay
- It's okay to not be okay

21:59.234 --> 22:02.696
- It's okay
- It's okay

22:02.779 --> 22:06.700
- It's okay to be sick at heart
- It's okay to be sick at heart

22:06.783 --> 22:10.078
- I'm really okay
- I'm really okay

22:10.162 --> 22:13.582
- It's not because of the director
- It's not because of the director

22:13.832 --> 22:17.169
- It's not because of my medicine
- It's not because of my medicine

22:17.252 --> 22:20.839
- I'm okay because I'm strong
- I'm okay because I'm strong

22:20.922 --> 22:24.551
- I'm really okay
- I'm really okay

22:24.634 --> 22:25.802
I love you guys.

22:28.347 --> 22:29.556
THERAPY ROOM

22:39.524 --> 22:41.151
It's sunny outside.

22:41.818 --> 22:44.237
Why don't we go for a walk?

22:53.997 --> 22:57.167
Sang-tae, I have plans today,
so I'm going to be a bit late.

22:57.918 --> 23:01.463
So wait for me at Jae-su's.
I'll go pick you up in the evening.

23:01.546 --> 23:05.008
"We really click, Sang-tae.
We're like best friends."

23:06.009 --> 23:07.886
- What?
- Best friends.

23:07.969 --> 23:10.764
Ms. Ko and I are best friends now.

23:10.847 --> 23:14.267
That means we're buddies and besties.
It means we're really close.

23:14.351 --> 23:18.146
Your best friend is Jae-su.
My best friend is Ms. Ko.

23:19.022 --> 23:22.859
I also have a best friend now.
I have a best friend.

23:27.322 --> 23:28.824
Don't you miss your daughter?

23:29.449 --> 23:31.201
I heard her fairy tale class is
really fun.

23:31.785 --> 23:33.995
Maybe I should watch her teach one day.

23:37.082 --> 23:40.252
She's just like that woman.

23:41.628 --> 23:43.672
- "That woman"?
- Everyone

23:45.590 --> 23:47.384
got fooled by that woman.

23:48.969 --> 23:50.762
She has the face of an angel.

23:51.888 --> 23:53.640
But there lives a demon inside.

23:55.559 --> 24:00.564
Everyone is good and bad.
We all live with both traits.

24:02.149 --> 24:03.608
That woman is a monster.

24:05.026 --> 24:06.194
She killed someone.

24:08.071 --> 24:09.573
I'm telling you. She killed someone.

24:10.949 --> 24:13.869
Where is that monster?

24:15.328 --> 24:16.454
She's dead.

24:17.164 --> 24:18.165
I killed her.

24:28.508 --> 24:29.634
I'm sure

24:30.802 --> 24:31.761
I killed her.

24:32.345 --> 24:33.680
But she came back.

24:35.223 --> 24:36.433
She came back to kill me.

24:38.101 --> 24:39.519
She's going to kill me.

24:50.197 --> 24:51.198
THE MURDER OF THE WITCH OF THE WEST

24:53.658 --> 24:54.951
Ms. Park Ok-ran.

24:56.161 --> 24:57.829
You're not allowed in here.

24:57.913 --> 24:59.664
Why were you reading this

25:00.540 --> 25:02.375
when I wasn't done reading it myself?

25:05.462 --> 25:07.923
Well, I was just...

25:11.885 --> 25:12.886
See?

25:13.720 --> 25:15.805
It's because you touched something
that wasn't yours.

25:16.848 --> 25:18.058
I hate it

25:19.351 --> 25:20.477
when people do that.

25:32.489 --> 25:33.573
Are you okay?

25:34.616 --> 25:37.244
Yes, I'm okay. It's just a paper cut.

25:37.327 --> 25:39.037
- I'll give you a bandage.
- No, it's okay.

25:39.996 --> 25:42.958
By the way, I noticed that
Mr. Joo Jeong-tae went outside today.

25:43.375 --> 25:44.668
Wasn't it Mr. Kan Pil-ong's turn?

25:45.377 --> 25:46.294
Yes.

25:46.795 --> 25:50.423
But Director O signed a permit
for Mr. Joo Jeong-tae this morning.

25:52.717 --> 25:55.011
I bet someone made a deal
behind the curtain.

25:55.845 --> 25:56.930
"A deal"?

25:59.224 --> 26:00.517
Are you ready?

26:02.519 --> 26:03.395
I'm going in, okay?

26:19.869 --> 26:20.954
Are you doing a circus show?

26:21.037 --> 26:22.622
Are you running away?

26:23.540 --> 26:25.667
I mean...
Can't you wear something comfortable?

26:26.251 --> 26:27.669
I feel comfortable naked.

26:28.295 --> 26:29.546
Don't you have anything normal?

26:29.629 --> 26:31.464
- I don't want to look normal.
- Why not?

26:34.301 --> 26:35.343
Because it's normal.

26:37.304 --> 26:39.347
- At least wear comfortable shoes--
- What did you pack?

26:44.060 --> 26:45.020
Are we evacuating?

26:45.103 --> 26:48.273
Well, we might get hungry
when we're outside...

26:50.233 --> 26:51.568
My goodness.

26:53.611 --> 26:55.322
Did a patient call you or something?

26:56.448 --> 27:00.952
I just thought we might need it
just in case...

27:01.036 --> 27:02.329
Don't make it so obvious

27:02.829 --> 27:04.497
that this your first time going somewhere.

27:08.960 --> 27:11.129
You just need to take care of me.

27:19.304 --> 27:21.348
- Don't pick up.
- Hello?

27:22.474 --> 27:23.725
Who is that jerk?

27:24.225 --> 27:26.227
Two club sandwiches, please.

27:33.026 --> 27:34.778
You should eat it while it's warm.

27:35.278 --> 27:36.780
You had something urgent to tell me?

27:36.863 --> 27:38.907
I can't talk properly when I'm hungry.

27:42.535 --> 27:43.370
Do you have plans?

27:44.913 --> 27:45.830
Yes.

27:46.706 --> 27:47.832
A date with Ms. Ko?

27:51.586 --> 27:53.088
I told you already.

27:54.130 --> 27:57.300
I'm amazing
when it comes to reading people's minds.

28:00.929 --> 28:01.930
Then

28:03.139 --> 28:04.766
can I ask you something?

28:07.602 --> 28:08.686
Go ahead.

28:12.107 --> 28:14.818
What's the psychology
behind people who overdress

28:14.901 --> 28:17.695
and wear things that are way too fancy?

28:20.698 --> 28:21.825
I'm guessing it's because

28:22.617 --> 28:24.661
they want to show off, right?

28:29.874 --> 28:32.544
It's the opposite.
They want to protect themselves.

28:33.545 --> 28:36.047
They think they're too weak,
so they use clothes for protection.

28:37.549 --> 28:39.551
It's like an armor.

28:42.554 --> 28:47.058
So you should do a good job
of protecting her.

28:47.142 --> 28:48.601
I'm talking about Ms. Ko.

28:57.444 --> 28:58.987
My best friend...

28:59.654 --> 29:02.031
When... When are we
going to have our meeting?

29:02.115 --> 29:03.491
- Sang-tae.
- Yes?

29:03.575 --> 29:05.452
What kind of women
did Gang-tae hang out with?

29:08.872 --> 29:13.042
Nurses, patients,

29:13.126 --> 29:16.546
teachers at my school, landlords...

29:16.629 --> 29:19.674
No, I'm not talking about
those kinds of women.

29:20.175 --> 29:22.385
- What kind of women does he like?
- He doesn't like women.

29:23.511 --> 29:26.222
- Does he like men?
- He likes me.

29:26.306 --> 29:30.018
"You're my favorite person
in the whole world, Sang-tae."

29:30.101 --> 29:31.936
Gang-tae only hangs out with me.

29:33.062 --> 29:35.690
No wonder he doesn't know how to have fun.

29:39.444 --> 29:41.070
I should make sure he has a blast.

29:41.154 --> 29:42.739
No. Mang-tae.

29:44.073 --> 29:45.575
I gave you Mang-tae.

29:46.201 --> 29:48.578
- What?
- You can play with Mang-tae.

29:48.661 --> 29:49.954
Gang-tae will play with me.

29:50.038 --> 29:52.373
And I... I will play with my best friend.

29:52.457 --> 29:54.542
- Can't I play with Gang-tae?
- No, you can't.

29:54.626 --> 29:57.337
Gang-tae can only have fun with me.
He's my little brother.

30:00.423 --> 30:01.549
Do you also adore Gang-tae?

30:01.633 --> 30:04.093
Yes, I really adore him.

30:04.969 --> 30:07.722
He... He has beautiful eyes.
He has the most beautiful eyes ever.

30:09.224 --> 30:10.517
Have you ever hated him?

30:17.565 --> 30:18.733
I guess you have.

30:19.359 --> 30:21.611
When did you hate Gang-tae?

30:25.907 --> 30:27.075
Aren't you going to tell me?

30:32.038 --> 30:32.872
Sang-tae.

30:33.706 --> 30:36.668
Do you know the story called
King Donkey Ears?

30:36.751 --> 30:40.421
Yes, the guy goes into the bamboo forest
and shouts,

30:40.505 --> 30:42.632
"The king has donkey ears!"

30:42.715 --> 30:45.426
Yes, that's right.
If you keep a secret to yourself,

30:45.510 --> 30:47.554
you end up getting frustrated.

30:47.637 --> 30:50.139
You need to tell someone
in order to relieve your stress.

30:53.810 --> 30:55.436
When did you hate Gang-tae the most?

31:04.153 --> 31:05.363
My phone is...

31:05.822 --> 31:07.240
Hey, Jae-su.

31:09.075 --> 31:10.201
I need to talk on the phone.

31:24.507 --> 31:27.635
Maybe you were right about that.

31:28.595 --> 31:31.973
You said that Ms. Ko's mother
may not be someone whom she misses

31:33.182 --> 31:35.351
but someone whom she still fears.

31:36.436 --> 31:38.021
It's just my guess.

31:38.104 --> 31:42.442
We can't trust everything
that a dementia patient says,

31:42.734 --> 31:45.570
but that doesn't mean we can entirely
rule out the possibility.

31:46.279 --> 31:47.113
What if

31:48.072 --> 31:50.575
the writer Do Hui-jae actually isn't dead?

31:51.451 --> 31:52.619
What if she just disappeared?

31:52.702 --> 31:53.995
Then we know one thing for sure.

31:54.746 --> 31:58.875
She'll definitely come back
to see her husband and daughter.

32:00.460 --> 32:03.046
Let's hope I'm worried for nothing,

32:04.839 --> 32:06.382
but just in case,

32:07.091 --> 32:08.426
I wanted to ask you

32:09.302 --> 32:12.138
to protect Ms. Ko and be there for her.

32:18.519 --> 32:19.854
"NONSTOP" BY OH MY GIRL

32:22.899 --> 32:25.401
Your brother is very calculating.

32:26.945 --> 32:27.779
What do you mean?

32:27.862 --> 32:31.115
He's all about give and take.
He doesn't give away anything for free.

32:32.825 --> 32:35.745
Isn't that why you guys are best friends?
Because you two are alike.

32:58.476 --> 32:59.811
Aren't you scared of riding motorcycles?

32:59.894 --> 33:01.354
No, it doesn't. Hand me the helmet.

33:02.063 --> 33:03.189
It's so scary.

33:03.272 --> 33:04.691
- Jeez.
- Super scary!

33:06.776 --> 33:07.777
Wait up!

33:10.446 --> 33:12.323
Isn't it so nice to be home for a change?

33:12.407 --> 33:14.951
Ms. Kang will throw a samgyeopsal party
for you this evening.

33:15.576 --> 33:17.286
Why are you following me, Jae-su?

33:17.954 --> 33:18.871
To hang out with you.

33:20.581 --> 33:21.582
So you want me to leave?

33:22.667 --> 33:24.585
You're so mean.

33:24.961 --> 33:26.546
I closed up the restaurant for the day

33:26.629 --> 33:28.423
and drove Alberto
all the way up the mountain

33:28.506 --> 33:30.299
in this heatwave just to pick you up.

33:30.383 --> 33:31.592
Right. You did that, boss.

33:31.676 --> 33:34.095
Yes! I am your boss.

33:34.178 --> 33:37.724
What kind of part-timer wants to hang out
with his boss at his place?

33:44.772 --> 33:45.606
What?

33:47.984 --> 33:50.653
What's that?
Is Ms. Kang making kimchi already?

33:50.737 --> 33:52.030
Kimchi is made in the winter.

33:52.113 --> 33:53.906
November 7th is the first day of winter.

33:58.077 --> 33:59.704
My, I feel so refreshed.

34:00.580 --> 34:02.874
Gosh, our very own illustrator

34:04.167 --> 34:05.918
Mr. Moon is here.

34:06.002 --> 34:09.130
Hello! Mr. Lee Sang-in,
the CEO of SangSangESang Publishers.

34:09.213 --> 34:11.007
- Hello.
- What on earth are you doing here

34:11.090 --> 34:13.760
half-naked in broad daylight?

34:13.843 --> 34:15.511
As you can see, I'm enjoying my vacation.

34:15.595 --> 34:19.223
Usually, I book a resort overseas
every summer

34:19.307 --> 34:21.559
and do nothing but read books
for about a month.

34:21.642 --> 34:25.104
This was not planned, but I ended up
spending my summer like this here.

34:27.607 --> 34:29.984
Mr. Moon, take a dip.

34:30.068 --> 34:31.861
- It's so refreshing.
- No, I don't want to.

34:31.944 --> 34:33.279
I don't like water. I hate water.

34:33.362 --> 34:34.864
Jeez, why did you do that?

34:34.947 --> 34:36.699
Wait, Sang-tae. Wait up!

34:43.122 --> 34:44.290
Where are we headed?

34:44.457 --> 34:46.084
You wanted to see
the mountains and fields.

34:46.459 --> 34:47.877
Then I guess the mountains first?

35:05.269 --> 35:07.563
Is this the deviation
you've been dreaming of?

35:08.439 --> 35:11.359
Are we going to tie a rope
around our ankle and jump or something?

35:12.985 --> 35:13.986
Shall we?

35:15.363 --> 35:17.073
- Let's go.
- No.

35:18.324 --> 35:19.325
Why not?

35:19.742 --> 35:20.576
I'm scared.

35:23.329 --> 35:24.789
- Why are you laughing?
- Well...

35:25.331 --> 35:26.749
Hearing you say the word, "scared"--

35:26.833 --> 35:27.834
You think it's funny?

35:28.251 --> 35:30.336
Do you think it'll be fun
to cross this stupid bridge?

35:33.297 --> 35:34.298
I just

35:35.258 --> 35:37.802
wanted to come up high
and enjoy an open view.

35:39.637 --> 35:41.055
I can't come here with Sang-tae.

35:45.685 --> 35:46.894
I saw it, so it's all good now.

35:47.270 --> 35:48.104
Let's go back down.

35:48.980 --> 35:50.064
So you're saying

35:50.898 --> 35:52.567
you can't hang out
with Sang-tae like this?

35:54.110 --> 35:55.945
Okay, fine. Let's do this.

35:59.448 --> 36:00.449
But carry me on your back.

36:04.954 --> 36:06.706
Wait here. I'll be right back.

36:08.749 --> 36:10.710
Hey! Carry me on your back!

36:11.335 --> 36:13.546
I said, carry me!
Give me a piggyback ride!

36:14.213 --> 36:16.090
Darn it. Crap.

36:19.760 --> 36:21.220
Shit! It's shaky.

36:23.139 --> 36:24.765
That's why it's called the Shaky Bridge.

36:25.099 --> 36:26.392
Why is it freaking shaky?

36:28.144 --> 36:28.978
Wait up.

36:29.687 --> 36:31.314
Why don't you sing a song
if you're scared?

36:31.772 --> 36:32.773
A song?

36:36.068 --> 36:37.570
If I

36:38.404 --> 36:40.406
Feel lonely

36:41.699 --> 36:42.783
If I

36:42.867 --> 36:43.701
Stop.

36:44.493 --> 36:45.494
Why?

36:46.329 --> 36:47.205
You sound scary.

36:47.330 --> 36:48.331
Do you have a death wish?

36:50.958 --> 36:52.335
If I

36:52.919 --> 36:54.086
Gosh, I'm hungry.

36:54.420 --> 36:55.671
What will you feed me?

36:57.423 --> 36:58.758
Since we're in the mountains...

36:59.342 --> 37:00.426
How about raw squid?

37:00.718 --> 37:02.511
- What?
- Well, let's see.

37:02.595 --> 37:04.096
Is there a good restaurant nearby?

37:10.978 --> 37:13.356
Go stand over there.
I'll take a picture of you.

37:13.940 --> 37:14.774
You said you're hungry.

37:15.441 --> 37:16.275
Come on.

37:22.490 --> 37:24.116
- Hurry up.
- Smile.

37:27.078 --> 37:28.829
I told you to smile, not cry.

37:29.413 --> 37:30.539
Just take it, will you?

37:32.041 --> 37:33.251
Strike a cool pose.

37:43.844 --> 37:45.346
Enough. I don't want photos.

37:45.805 --> 37:47.765
Okay. If it's embarrassing,
I'll take it with you.

37:47.848 --> 37:48.683
Sit back down.

37:50.393 --> 37:51.310
Sit down.

37:53.104 --> 37:54.897
One, two, three.

37:56.857 --> 37:59.193
Smile. Don't cry.

38:10.538 --> 38:11.372
Hello?

38:18.921 --> 38:20.965
We were told to expect someone
who can help us from the west.

38:21.549 --> 38:22.842
It was true.

38:23.884 --> 38:25.177
My gosh.

38:27.555 --> 38:28.389
What is going...

38:31.434 --> 38:32.393
Can you explain this?

38:32.977 --> 38:35.187
Oh, what happened was...

38:35.855 --> 38:37.982
You know, I'm supposed
to stay out overnight tomorrow.

38:38.065 --> 38:39.900
Can Jeong-tae go instead? Joo Jeong-tae.

38:42.695 --> 38:43.571
A-reum!

38:44.530 --> 38:46.824
We just got into a taxi

38:46.907 --> 38:48.659
and said we'd go as far as we could.

38:49.618 --> 38:51.370
That's why we ended up here.

38:51.454 --> 38:54.332
181,800 WON

39:04.800 --> 39:07.136
CHEAP GUESTHOUSE
300M

39:09.764 --> 39:12.016
We spent all the money we had
on the taxi ride,

39:12.099 --> 39:13.893
so we couldn't pay for the room.

39:14.852 --> 39:16.812
- We're totally broke.
- That's right.

39:18.647 --> 39:19.899
How did you get my number?

39:22.651 --> 39:25.029
This reads,
"Call in case of an emergency."

39:28.699 --> 39:30.076
EMERGENCY CONTACTS

39:30.659 --> 39:32.828
Out of everyone here,
you're the closest to me.

39:34.997 --> 39:36.957
Spending time with a patient
outside the hospital--

39:37.041 --> 39:39.627
It's not allowed.
I know that it's against the rules.

39:39.835 --> 39:41.837
So just lend us some money
to pay for the room.

39:42.463 --> 39:44.090
It was hard for me to get out for a night.

39:45.174 --> 39:47.218
I'll stay here with A-reum
just for the night

39:47.301 --> 39:48.719
and return to the hospital tomorrow.

39:49.762 --> 39:51.180
They also accept credit cards.

39:54.850 --> 39:55.976
No, I can't do that.

39:57.103 --> 39:58.145
- Why not?
- Why can't you?

39:58.229 --> 39:59.939
Strictly speaking, this is all your fault.

40:00.523 --> 40:02.149
Patients can't date one another,

40:02.233 --> 40:04.276
so you told me
to just hold back my feelings.

40:04.360 --> 40:06.487
- So I listened to you and did just that.
- Right.

40:06.570 --> 40:09.115
But when A-reum's ex-husband
slapped Ms. Ko in the face,

40:09.615 --> 40:11.575
- what did you do?
- He didn't hold himself back.

40:13.119 --> 40:14.078
Well, in that moment--

40:14.161 --> 40:16.205
Because you punched him,

40:16.288 --> 40:18.332
A-reum's parents came to see her
at the hospital,

40:18.416 --> 40:19.500
and they discharged her.

40:19.583 --> 40:21.335
That means we will have to
part ways tomorrow.

40:23.129 --> 40:25.214
And you can't even pay
for us to stay here for a night?

40:28.342 --> 40:29.301
This is so cruel.

40:30.094 --> 40:31.762
Very cruel, indeed.

40:34.723 --> 40:35.724
Apologize to them.

40:37.476 --> 40:38.894
It looks like it was your fault.

40:39.645 --> 40:41.313
I paid for the room next to theirs.

40:44.608 --> 40:45.776
Hey.

40:50.448 --> 40:52.074
I told you that we can't stay overnight.

40:53.367 --> 40:54.952
My gosh, are you Cinderella or what?

40:59.081 --> 41:00.458
Sleep here by yourself.

41:01.625 --> 41:03.002
I bet they'll elope tomorrow.

41:03.961 --> 41:06.130
The woman will move to the States soon,

41:06.714 --> 41:09.800
and the man has to return
to the psychiatric hospital tomorrow.

41:10.843 --> 41:12.303
I mean, look at those eyes.

41:12.595 --> 41:14.305
Do you think they can be apart?

41:17.183 --> 41:20.728
Your rationality can never win
against your desires.

41:25.149 --> 41:28.068
Will you let the patient run away?
How irresponsible.

41:29.361 --> 41:32.865
Or will you break them apart
despite knowing how in love they are?

41:33.866 --> 41:34.700
That's so cruel.

41:37.453 --> 41:39.371
Let's just stay with them here tonight.

41:40.206 --> 41:42.875
That way, you can take him back
to the hospital tomorrow.

41:43.334 --> 41:44.335
Right, Mr. Caregiver?

41:53.969 --> 41:55.137
I've been

41:55.763 --> 41:57.014
suspended from work,

41:58.098 --> 41:59.099
so I refuse to work.

42:10.694 --> 42:13.072
See? We're so screwed.

42:13.572 --> 42:14.865
We'll be okay, A-reum.

42:25.501 --> 42:26.502
All right.

42:26.627 --> 42:28.295
Do you guys know
when Gang-tae will be here?

42:28.379 --> 42:30.673
It'd be nice if he could join us.

42:30.756 --> 42:33.842
- Well, he'll get here pretty late.
- Did he get a part-time job again?

42:33.926 --> 42:35.594
No, he had to meet someone.

42:35.678 --> 42:36.512
Who?

42:36.595 --> 42:38.639
Oh, I'm sure he's out
meeting up with people he knows.

42:38.722 --> 42:40.599
He has lots of time
now that he's been suspended,

42:40.683 --> 42:43.519
- so he's probably out clearing his head.
- Gosh, that's good.

42:44.019 --> 42:46.647
When will he get to take it easy
if not now?

42:47.022 --> 42:49.191
My gosh,
you've been grilling meat nonstop.

42:49.441 --> 42:51.193
Here, Ju-ri. Have some.

42:51.277 --> 42:52.736
I'll eat it myself.

42:54.113 --> 42:57.533
Gosh, this is embarrassing.
Even my arm is getting tired.

42:57.616 --> 42:59.076
Don't be like that. Just eat this.

42:59.159 --> 43:00.077
Here.

43:00.160 --> 43:01.912
Why are you being like this, seriously?

43:10.296 --> 43:12.965
Are you enjoying working with Ms. Ko?

43:13.048 --> 43:14.466
We will work later.

43:14.550 --> 43:16.927
"Later" means sometime before you die.

43:17.011 --> 43:18.804
What? Before you die?

43:19.638 --> 43:22.391
Jeez, so she's working on a book
that will be published posthumously?

43:23.183 --> 43:25.019
Gosh, Mun-yeong...

43:25.686 --> 43:27.313
Have you two gotten quite close?

43:27.563 --> 43:29.189
Yes, we're best friends now.

43:29.273 --> 43:31.108
Best friends don't keep secrets
from each other.

43:31.609 --> 43:33.068
Then you should've brought her.

43:33.152 --> 43:35.362
I told her I'd love
to invite her over for a meal one day.

43:35.446 --> 43:37.823
She said no.
She went somewhere fun by herself.

43:37.906 --> 43:40.701
I... I would've been happy
to hang out with her.

43:41.201 --> 43:42.620
You didn't want to hang out with me.

43:42.703 --> 43:44.997
You're really hurting my feelings,
Sang-tae.

43:45.080 --> 43:46.999
That's very odd.

43:47.082 --> 43:50.002
She wouldn't want to go out in this heat.

43:50.085 --> 43:53.172
Maybe they went together.
Ms. Ko and Mr. Moon Gang-tae.

44:07.186 --> 44:09.063
You sure work in publishing.

44:09.146 --> 44:14.151
You're incredibly creative, Seung-jae.

44:15.027 --> 44:16.028
Right? She really is.

44:16.111 --> 44:18.697
Hey, maybe I should have you sign
a publishing contract as a writer.

44:21.617 --> 44:25.871
Well, how about a beer for everyone?

44:25.954 --> 44:27.039
I'd love that.

44:27.122 --> 44:28.248
I'll go.

44:33.712 --> 44:35.464
I'll give her a hand.

44:38.801 --> 44:41.637
Mr. Lee, do you mind picking up
some coffee milk for me?

44:41.720 --> 44:42.680
You crazy little brat...

44:48.394 --> 44:50.938
They're probably together now, right?

44:53.273 --> 44:55.025
Gang-tae and Mun-yeong.

44:56.193 --> 44:57.194
Not sure.

44:58.404 --> 45:00.197
And who cares?

45:00.447 --> 45:03.158
I mean, you're with me now.

45:08.038 --> 45:12.751
I'm beginning to understand
why Mun-yeong has stuck around you

45:13.585 --> 45:14.753
for so long.

45:15.337 --> 45:16.839
That's a compliment, right?

45:20.050 --> 45:24.054
But to tell you the truth,
it's actually the other way around.

45:24.221 --> 45:26.390
I'm the one that's sticking around her.

45:28.100 --> 45:29.059
Why?

45:31.895 --> 45:33.230
Well...

45:35.315 --> 45:37.401
Because she cannot be left alone.

45:40.362 --> 45:41.989
She's very lonely.

45:43.657 --> 45:46.368
But she doesn't want anyone to know that,

45:46.452 --> 45:48.829
so she pushes people away.

45:49.663 --> 45:50.956
She's complicated.

45:59.548 --> 46:01.884
I have to say, they're so alike.

46:03.510 --> 46:07.389
Do you think that's why
they're attracted to each other?

46:09.558 --> 46:10.559
Ju-ri.

46:11.602 --> 46:13.979
There can be countless reasons

46:14.813 --> 46:16.648
as to why we fall for someone.

46:17.149 --> 46:19.193
For example, you might fall for
how pretty they look when they cry.

46:20.527 --> 46:23.113
Or you might fall for them
when they get drunk and swear at you.

46:23.197 --> 46:26.158
Or it might be when they
unexpectedly slap you in the face.

46:32.831 --> 46:34.041
Mr. Moon must've also

46:35.125 --> 46:36.210
found some kind of reason

46:38.003 --> 46:40.047
to fall for Mun-yeong.

47:00.234 --> 47:02.569
The owner of this guesthouse said
we can drink this.

47:02.653 --> 47:04.196
She made this fruit marmalade herself.

47:09.159 --> 47:10.869
You haven't called him yet?
Shall I call him?

47:10.953 --> 47:11.870
No, don't.

47:12.371 --> 47:13.580
I'll go call him now.

47:28.470 --> 47:29.346
Hey.

47:31.473 --> 47:32.307
Did you eat dinner?

47:33.308 --> 47:34.393
Yes, we had samgyeopsal.

47:34.518 --> 47:36.186
My gosh, you guys must've had a feast.

47:36.812 --> 47:37.896
What are you up to now?

47:38.564 --> 47:39.856
What are you up to?

47:40.440 --> 47:41.733
What? Me?

47:42.442 --> 47:43.986
Well, I'm...

47:47.573 --> 47:49.157
I'm chatting with you on the phone.

47:49.950 --> 47:51.159
When will you be back?

47:51.618 --> 47:55.539
Oh, I'll be back very late.

47:55.622 --> 47:58.083
Around midnight? Or around 1 or 2 a.m.?

48:00.168 --> 48:03.672
No, I may have to sleep here tonight.

48:04.506 --> 48:06.925
Don't wait for me.
Just go to bed, Sang-tae.

48:08.635 --> 48:11.221
And make sure you close the window screens
before you go to bed.

48:12.014 --> 48:13.432
Don't sleep on the floor.

48:14.141 --> 48:15.559
Also, make sure the fan is rotating.

48:18.228 --> 48:19.396
If you get bored

48:20.022 --> 48:21.648
or can't fall asleep, call me.

48:27.613 --> 48:28.739
You too.

48:30.991 --> 48:32.534
Call me if you get bored.

48:55.807 --> 48:57.851
Oh, I've seen that face on TV dramas.

48:58.477 --> 48:59.311
What do you mean?

48:59.895 --> 49:01.688
The face of a man
who is cheating on his wife.

49:09.488 --> 49:11.031
I don't want to be a mistress.

49:11.114 --> 49:12.282
I want to be a faithful wife.

49:12.366 --> 49:13.450
But those two

49:14.034 --> 49:15.535
can't be best friends, can they?

49:21.625 --> 49:22.751
Sang-tae was happy

49:24.002 --> 49:25.337
about being best friends with you.

49:28.131 --> 49:29.174
Well...

49:30.175 --> 49:31.677
I'm also fond of your brother.

49:32.678 --> 49:33.720
He's cute.

49:43.897 --> 49:45.190
There was something

49:47.234 --> 49:49.152
my mom wished for her whole life.

49:52.197 --> 49:53.615
Seeing Sang-tae with a friend.

49:58.245 --> 50:00.205
A real friend who truly understands him.

50:02.165 --> 50:03.125
Just one.

50:09.423 --> 50:11.299
I had a friend like that
a long time ago as well.

50:13.593 --> 50:14.720
A friend who understands me.

50:27.733 --> 50:31.611
THE BOY WHO FED ON NIGHTMARES

50:33.363 --> 50:35.991
- Nam Ju-ri!
- Nam Ju-ri!

50:36.074 --> 50:38.702
- Nam Ju-ri!
- Nam Ju-ri!

50:38.785 --> 50:41.288
- Nam Ju-ri!
- Nam Ju-ri!

50:41.371 --> 50:44.124
- Nam Ju-ri!
- Nam Ju-ri!

50:44.207 --> 50:45.417
- Nam Ju-ri!
- Gosh!

50:46.293 --> 50:48.462
- Look at that!
- Hilarious!

50:48.545 --> 50:49.629
What an idiot.

50:49.713 --> 50:50.839
That girl

50:51.715 --> 50:54.301
- was afraid of her classmates.
- Nam Ju-ri is a crybaby

50:54.384 --> 50:57.512
- Nam Ju-ri is a crybaby
- Nam Ju-ri is a crybaby

50:57.596 --> 51:00.724
- Nam Ju-ri is an idiot
- Nam Ju-ri is an idiot

51:00.807 --> 51:01.933
But those kids

51:02.976 --> 51:04.269
were afraid of me.

51:20.827 --> 51:21.828
Get lost.

51:21.912 --> 51:24.623
Hey. Shall we

51:24.706 --> 51:27.501
become friends?

51:33.632 --> 51:35.675
I liked it because I was no longer bored.

51:36.635 --> 51:37.552
And she liked it

51:37.844 --> 51:40.347
because her classmates
no longer bullied her.

51:43.600 --> 51:44.976
But the thing is...

51:45.060 --> 51:46.019
Ready or not!

51:46.102 --> 51:48.897
- Rock-paper-scissors! I won!
- She didn't want just one friend.

51:50.065 --> 51:52.234
She wanted to be everyone's friend.

51:53.652 --> 51:54.736
And I

51:55.779 --> 51:57.614
- didn't like that.
- We won!

51:59.282 --> 52:00.283
So?

52:02.786 --> 52:04.287
Did you harass those kids?

52:05.163 --> 52:06.164
Yes.

52:07.082 --> 52:08.917
I thought she'd only be friends with me

52:09.751 --> 52:11.962
if she became lonely again.

52:12.462 --> 52:13.713
Let's do it together.

52:21.012 --> 52:22.681
What do you think? Did I do a good job?

52:40.615 --> 52:42.117
But I was wrong.

52:54.004 --> 52:56.339
Don't... Don't come close.

52:59.634 --> 53:00.802
Go away.

53:03.555 --> 53:04.639
I said, go away!

53:08.852 --> 53:10.103
Please.

53:11.688 --> 53:13.273
Please go away.

53:29.706 --> 53:32.125
A friend who truly understands you

53:34.044 --> 53:35.378
does not exist.

53:37.547 --> 53:38.924
You should reconcile with her.

53:39.507 --> 53:40.550
I don't want to.

53:42.886 --> 53:46.014
- Why not?
- Because I have a best friend now.

53:50.518 --> 53:51.811
And I also have you.

53:55.774 --> 53:56.608
Hey.

53:58.234 --> 53:59.235
Your cheeks are...

53:59.319 --> 54:00.528
Goodness.

54:10.789 --> 54:12.332
- What's wrong?
- This is booze.

54:12.415 --> 54:13.249
What?

54:14.042 --> 54:16.127
No, the lady said
it's raspberry marmalade.

54:16.211 --> 54:18.505
I guess she didn't put in enough sugar.

54:20.423 --> 54:21.716
No, Jeong-tae!

54:22.550 --> 54:23.718
I won't drink this.

54:23.802 --> 54:25.929
You saw me spitting it out just now.

54:39.693 --> 54:40.568
Hey.

54:42.612 --> 54:44.155
Go sleep in the other room

54:44.572 --> 54:46.116
and send Jeong-tae here.

54:46.199 --> 54:48.994
Those lovebirds
have to part ways tomorrow,

54:49.077 --> 54:50.245
so just leave them be.

54:54.374 --> 54:55.458
Don't turn your back on me.

55:07.846 --> 55:09.389
I see that you smile a lot like an idiot

55:09.472 --> 55:11.057
when you're drunk.

55:15.687 --> 55:16.896
I have fun

55:17.856 --> 55:18.857
when I'm with you.

55:23.278 --> 55:24.612
I keep on smiling.

55:29.576 --> 55:30.660
This won't do.

55:32.203 --> 55:33.038
What do you mean?

55:36.499 --> 55:37.834
- Hey.
- What's the matter?

55:38.251 --> 55:39.919
- Come here.
- Why are you being like this?

55:40.003 --> 55:41.880
- Who's more in love?
- Calm down, please.

55:42.380 --> 55:43.965
The one who's more patient.

55:44.049 --> 55:45.175
- Ko Mun-yeong!
- Moon Gang-tae!

55:46.259 --> 55:47.218
Why?

55:48.720 --> 55:51.639
Because love is all about patience.

56:09.282 --> 56:11.284
Okay, fine. Let go of me now.

56:11.367 --> 56:12.243
I'll just go to sleep.

56:15.455 --> 56:17.082
I said I'll go to sleep.

56:31.930 --> 56:33.139
Please.

56:34.307 --> 56:35.892
Stay still and just go to sleep.

56:42.023 --> 56:43.566
Come on. Just sleep.

56:45.819 --> 56:47.570
I heard you can fall asleep easily

56:48.780 --> 56:50.615
when someone caresses your hair.

57:34.993 --> 57:36.870
CHEAP GUESTHOUSE

57:48.381 --> 57:50.008
I told you

57:53.553 --> 57:54.804
that I can no longer

57:57.182 --> 57:58.808
hold myself back.

58:05.690 --> 58:06.733
I guess

58:09.944 --> 58:11.529
I can't run away anymore.

58:26.878 --> 58:30.465
Don't go. Don't leave me, Mom.

58:31.424 --> 58:34.552
Gang-tae, I'm here.

58:35.637 --> 58:38.723
I'm here. Don't leave me.

59:03.498 --> 59:04.749
Moon Gang-tae!

59:09.504 --> 59:10.713
Moon Gang-tae!

59:18.054 --> 59:19.305
Don't go.

59:19.597 --> 59:21.015
Don't go...

59:34.070 --> 59:34.904
MY BROTHER

59:44.247 --> 59:45.748
The number you have dialed...

59:55.550 --> 59:56.551
Moon Gang-tae!

59:59.470 --> 01:00:00.346
Moon Gang-tae...

01:00:16.821 --> 01:00:17.989
Where were you?

01:00:19.115 --> 01:00:19.949
Well...

01:00:22.493 --> 01:00:24.120
To get what I couldn't give you last time.

01:00:24.787 --> 01:00:25.622
What?

01:00:40.053 --> 01:00:41.346
Don't trample on them this time.

01:00:43.681 --> 01:00:44.974
They're beautiful.

01:00:48.853 --> 01:00:49.687
So are you.

01:02:28.453 --> 01:02:30.747
Oh, you guys are still here.

01:02:30.830 --> 01:02:33.249
The other couple
left early in the morning.

01:02:33.332 --> 01:02:35.418
Pardon me?
Their shoes are still here though.

01:02:36.669 --> 01:02:37.754
I have no idea.

01:02:42.049 --> 01:02:42.884
Gang-tae.

01:02:52.310 --> 01:02:55.813
With this, we can stay together for
a month without worrying about anything.

01:02:56.689 --> 01:02:58.566
I thought we'd have to part ways
in the morning,

01:02:58.649 --> 01:03:00.359
so I didn't get any sleep last night.

01:03:01.027 --> 01:03:04.322
Who knew Ms. Ko would give us money
so that we could run away together?

01:03:04.572 --> 01:03:06.073
Isn't she so cool?

01:03:10.620 --> 01:03:12.288
- A-reum.
- What is it?

01:03:12.371 --> 01:03:13.581
I really don't think

01:03:14.624 --> 01:03:15.875
this is right.

01:03:16.459 --> 01:03:17.835
What do you mean?

01:03:17.919 --> 01:03:19.253
Running away like this

01:03:20.171 --> 01:03:22.924
will turn our love into nothing
but a petty and cowardly act.

01:03:24.509 --> 01:03:26.302
- What are you talking about?
- You see...

01:03:27.428 --> 01:03:29.680
The truth is,
I still go crazy when I see alcohol.

01:03:30.473 --> 01:03:32.308
Even last night,
I struggled to restrain myself.

01:03:33.684 --> 01:03:35.144
Had you not been with me,

01:03:35.228 --> 01:03:37.021
I would've drunk until I dropped.

01:03:38.439 --> 01:03:39.273
I have not yet

01:03:40.858 --> 01:03:42.944
recovered enough to take care of you

01:03:44.487 --> 01:03:46.239
and be responsible for your happiness.

01:03:47.573 --> 01:03:50.117
We can just try our best together.

01:04:00.294 --> 01:04:03.256
No, I need to get through this on my own.

01:04:04.382 --> 01:04:05.591
I will get through this.

01:04:06.717 --> 01:04:08.302
I promise you that I'll fully recover

01:04:09.262 --> 01:04:10.763
and come to you.

01:04:12.515 --> 01:04:13.808
So please

01:04:17.520 --> 01:04:19.063
wait for me. I won't take long.

01:04:57.018 --> 01:05:00.980
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

01:05:08.446 --> 01:05:10.448
Thanks so much, Gang-tae.

01:05:10.531 --> 01:05:12.325
I owe you one.

01:05:21.459 --> 01:05:22.627
Is he a fool?

01:05:23.377 --> 01:05:25.254
Why let her go if he loves her?

01:05:25.838 --> 01:05:27.298
Because he loves her a lot.

01:05:29.050 --> 01:05:30.801
Sometimes, that's why
you must let someone go.

01:05:31.928 --> 01:05:33.804
So they broke up
because they love each other?

01:05:34.388 --> 01:05:35.473
That's complete bullshit.

01:05:38.517 --> 01:05:40.394
I will never let you go.

01:05:41.646 --> 01:05:42.980
Don't be so sure of it.

01:05:43.773 --> 01:05:45.399
You never know what could happen.

01:05:47.526 --> 01:05:49.028
I'll go check in on Sang-tae.

01:05:49.612 --> 01:05:51.572
Be quick.
I'll kill you if you take too long.

01:06:11.842 --> 01:06:12.718
Are you serious?

01:06:13.094 --> 01:06:15.429
Mr. Moon and Ms. Ko came together?

01:06:15.721 --> 01:06:19.141
Yes, he must've been
that special someone from the west.

01:06:19.433 --> 01:06:22.186
Thanks to them, A-reum and I
made some unforgettable memories.

01:06:22.269 --> 01:06:23.187
Really?

01:06:24.146 --> 01:06:26.899
That means they're seeing each other.

01:06:26.983 --> 01:06:28.109
Yes.

01:06:28.192 --> 01:06:30.403
It might be fun to plan a double wedding
down the road.

01:06:31.070 --> 01:06:33.030
- Would you officiate our wedding?
- My gosh.

01:06:33.114 --> 01:06:34.490
- Me?
- Yes.

01:06:43.165 --> 01:06:44.709
It's almost done.

01:06:45.418 --> 01:06:47.461
Why didn't you pick up?

01:06:47.753 --> 01:06:48.629
What?

01:06:51.007 --> 01:06:53.134
Oh, my phone is dead.

01:06:53.718 --> 01:06:54.552
You called?

01:06:54.635 --> 01:06:56.595
Yes, 4 times. No, 9... It was 17 times.

01:06:57.179 --> 01:06:58.973
Why? Did something happen?

01:07:03.185 --> 01:07:05.896
Where have you been? Where...

01:07:07.732 --> 01:07:09.108
I told you

01:07:09.191 --> 01:07:11.277
that I had to go to Seoul to see someone.

01:07:11.944 --> 01:07:13.446
By yourself?

01:07:14.030 --> 01:07:15.823
Yes, by myself.

01:07:20.202 --> 01:07:21.495
I can change the water for you.

01:07:21.579 --> 01:07:23.539
No, one must take care of one's own tasks.

01:07:23.622 --> 01:07:25.541
One must take care of one's own tasks.

01:07:25.624 --> 01:07:27.793
One must take care of one's own tasks.

01:07:42.933 --> 01:07:44.810
Big news! You need to hear this.

01:07:46.562 --> 01:07:49.607
Mr. O, please be quiet
when you're inside the hospital.

01:07:49.690 --> 01:07:52.401
Gosh, whatever. That's not important now.

01:07:53.319 --> 01:07:54.487
- Hey, follow me.
- Ms. Park.

01:07:55.112 --> 01:07:58.240
I'm going to tell you something,
but you two must keep it to yourselves.

01:08:08.292 --> 01:08:10.377
I'm starving. What's taking him so long?

01:08:32.358 --> 01:08:34.527
Dr. Kwon, you're a psychiatrist,

01:08:34.610 --> 01:08:36.278
so I can trust
that you're discreet, right?

01:08:37.029 --> 01:08:37.988
Yes, sure.

01:08:40.491 --> 01:08:43.285
What I'm about to tell you
must stay between us, okay?

01:08:45.329 --> 01:08:49.708
Mr. Moon Gang-tae and Ms. Ko Mun-yeong
are getting married soon.

01:08:49.792 --> 01:08:51.252
- What?
- Seriously, for real.

01:08:51.335 --> 01:08:54.004
Apparently, Mr. Joo Jeong-tae
saw them on a trip together.

01:08:54.088 --> 01:08:56.966
They even slept in the same room
at a guesthouse, so they're obviously...

01:09:26.078 --> 01:09:27.746
My gosh, that looks amazing.

01:09:32.001 --> 01:09:34.503
Did the three of you go on a trip
in a camping car?

01:09:35.379 --> 01:09:36.255
No.

01:09:37.715 --> 01:09:39.633
Then did you, by any chance,

01:09:40.050 --> 01:09:42.303
run into Mr. Joo Jeong-tae
outside the hospital?

01:09:45.139 --> 01:09:47.766
No, I ran into him
in front of the hospital.

01:09:47.850 --> 01:09:49.059
You're lying.

01:09:54.273 --> 01:09:55.941
I told you not to lie.

01:09:59.695 --> 01:10:02.072
Sang-tae, what's the matter?

01:10:05.743 --> 01:10:08.162
Who do you like more?
Me or Ms. Ko Mun-yeong?

01:10:12.374 --> 01:10:13.334
Why do you ask?

01:10:13.417 --> 01:10:15.586
Who do you like more?
Me or Ms. Ko Mun-yeong?

01:10:15.669 --> 01:10:18.214
My gosh. He likes you more, of course.

01:10:18.297 --> 01:10:22.176
I want you to answer my question.
Answer my question!

01:10:30.100 --> 01:10:31.060
Of course,

01:10:34.104 --> 01:10:35.397
I like you more.

01:10:41.070 --> 01:10:42.988
No, that's a lie.

01:10:43.781 --> 01:10:46.867
It's a lie. It's all a lie.

01:10:46.951 --> 01:10:48.494
- No, I mean it.
- It's a lie.

01:10:48.577 --> 01:10:49.828
I told you not to lie!

01:10:49.912 --> 01:10:53.457
Don't lie to me! It's all a lie.

01:10:56.293 --> 01:10:57.294
No.

01:10:58.587 --> 01:10:59.588
Sang-tae.

01:11:01.048 --> 01:11:02.132
I'm not lying.

01:11:05.803 --> 01:11:10.057
I'm sorry. It's my fault.

01:11:10.349 --> 01:11:12.851
I won't do it again, okay?

01:11:12.935 --> 01:11:14.687
"I want him to die.

01:11:17.106 --> 01:11:18.274
My brother...

01:11:19.483 --> 01:11:21.485
I just want my brother to die!

01:11:21.568 --> 01:11:24.363
I just want my brother to die."
You said that.

01:11:26.156 --> 01:11:28.158
You said you wanted me gone.

01:11:28.575 --> 01:11:31.954
You said to Mom every day
that you wanted me to die.

01:11:32.037 --> 01:11:34.999
That's why you pushed me into the river
that day.

01:11:36.834 --> 01:11:38.002
I shouted for help.

01:11:38.502 --> 01:11:41.422
I shouted... I kept crying for help,

01:11:41.505 --> 01:11:42.631
but you ran away.

01:11:42.715 --> 01:11:44.842
You left me alone in the water
and ran away.

01:11:45.134 --> 01:11:48.053
You wanted me dead. Every single day...

01:11:49.513 --> 01:11:51.598
I bet you wanted to kill me.

01:11:53.058 --> 01:11:54.643
- No...
- Everyone.

01:11:55.269 --> 01:12:01.275
Listen, everyone!
He's trying to kill his older brother!

01:12:02.526 --> 01:12:04.987
- No.
- Everyone!

01:12:05.612 --> 01:12:08.157
He's trying to kill his older brother!

01:12:08.240 --> 01:12:09.366
No...

01:12:11.118 --> 01:12:16.707
Listen, people! He is...
He's trying to kill his older brother!

01:12:16.790 --> 01:12:18.208
No, that's not true.

01:12:18.625 --> 01:12:19.668
No...

01:12:19.752 --> 01:12:22.129
- No...
- Listen, people!

01:12:23.297 --> 01:12:28.886
Everyone,
He's trying to kill his older brother!

01:12:30.012 --> 01:12:30.971
- No...
- Everyone, listen.

01:12:31.055 --> 01:12:33.223
- No.
- My brother...

01:12:33.307 --> 01:12:36.352
Listen,
he's trying to kill his older brother!

01:12:36.435 --> 01:12:37.436
No, that's not true.

01:12:38.937 --> 01:12:41.774
Listen to me.

01:12:41.857 --> 01:12:45.944
- Sang-tae, no.
- He's trying to kill his older brother!

01:12:47.279 --> 01:12:48.822
It's not true.

01:12:48.906 --> 01:12:50.407
No, that's not true.

01:12:52.076 --> 01:12:56.288
No, Sang-tae. That's not true.

01:12:56.372 --> 01:12:58.665
I'm not lying.

01:12:59.083 --> 01:13:00.876
Sang-tae.

01:13:42.876 --> 01:13:44.211
Why did you save me?

01:13:45.212 --> 01:13:46.588
You should've just left me to die.

01:13:48.465 --> 01:13:50.884
Try your best to stay strong. Who knows?

01:13:51.510 --> 01:13:53.387
Sang-tae might be the one
to help you one day.

01:13:53.470 --> 01:13:54.430
I...

01:13:55.681 --> 01:13:56.890
had a dream.

01:13:56.974 --> 01:13:57.850
What you just said

01:13:59.268 --> 01:14:00.227
sounds like you

01:14:01.103 --> 01:14:02.354
begging me to stop you.

01:14:04.189 --> 01:14:05.149
I miss him.

01:14:06.316 --> 01:14:09.528
It seems like you know
a lot about Do Hui-jae.

01:14:09.611 --> 01:14:12.614
Should I just kill him?

01:14:15.409 --> 01:14:17.744
Subtitle translation by Ja-won Lee
